  "upload": {
    "title": "Why McDonald's Ice Cream Machine Is Always Broken 🍦 #shorts",
    "description": "Most 'broken' McDonald's ice cream machines are mid-way through the Taylor machine's nightly heat-treatment cycle, which pasteurizes the mix and can take about four hours. When something fails, the machine locks up with vague error codes and only Taylor-authorized technicians can fix it. McBroken tracks machine status by ordering a sundae every 30 minutes; Kytch built a device to decode the errors, and in November 2020 McDonald's told franchisees to remove it. In October 2024 the U.S. Copyright Office granted a DMCA exemption so restaurants can legally bypass the digital locks to repair their own machines.",
